-- title:
--   Vanishing on the crossing chart forces divisibility by π
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Write $R_\pi = \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2, W) / (X_0 X_1 - C(\pi))$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W π`, and let $\mathrm{chartHom}\ \pi \colon W[[T]] \to R_\pi$ be the ring homomorphism obtained by substituting the distinguished ambient two-variable series attested by `hasSubst_sAmbient W` for the variable of the one-variable power series ring, followed by the quotient map `mk π`. The assertion is: for every one-variable power series $f \in W[[T]]$ whose image $\mathrm{chartHom}\ \pi\ f$ in $R_\pi$ is zero, there exists $g \in W[[T]]$ with $f = C(\pi)\, g$, where $C(\pi)$ denotes the constant power series $\pi$. Equivalently, the kernel of the chart homomorphism is contained in $\pi\, W[[T]]$: all coefficients of $f$ are divisible by $\pi$. No hypothesis on $\pi$ (such as being a non-zero-divisor) and no separatedness or completeness assumption on $W$ is imposed.
--
--   This is the divisibility step in the analysis of the chart of the ordinary double point model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$: a power series in the symmetric coordinate that dies in the crossing model has all coefficients divisible by $\pi$. It is used, by iteration, to prove [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.chartHom_injective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.chartHom_injective), the injectivity of the chart homomorphism over a $\pi$-adically separated base; the crossing model itself describes the completed local structure at a supersingular point of the $\Gamma_0(p)$-moduli problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_C_mul_of_chartHom_eq_zero.lean

